# 10. DECISION MEMORY

Build a structured decision-memory system.

A decision record should contain:

- Decision title.
- Decision.
- Reasoning.
- Date.
- Responsible person.
- Relevant role.
- Source.
- Supporting document.
- Related task.
- Follow-up date.
- Status.
- Revision history.

Users should be able to search decisions across their authorised contexts.

AI should answer questions such as:

"Why did I choose this option?"

"What did we agree at the last meeting?"

"Which decision is still waiting for approval?"

"Show me the latest decision related to this project."

Answers must cite the actual source records or links.

If the evidence is insufficient, the assistant must say so.

Do not invent a decision or present an AI suggestion as a confirmed human decision.

